mit_id":"99f71b3d50c60391a276505778d3daadcf9b70da","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thank you for being clear, that's a pretty fundamental thing to understand when working with these features though, so good to familiarize yourself with the way the engine API works!","created_at":"2026-04-26T12:42:38Z","updated_at":"2026-04-26T12:42:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118964#discussion_r3143489612","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118964","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3143489612"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118964#discussion_r3143489612"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118964"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3143489612/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":73,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3143470195,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3143618635","pull_request_review_id":4177028004,"id":3143618635,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc67X9BL","diff_hunk":"@@ -68,6 +68,30 @@ Error PacketPeerUDP::leave_multicast_group(IPAddress p_multi_address, const Stri\n \treturn _sock->leave_multicast_group(p_multi_address, p_if_name);\n }\n \n+Error PacketPeerUDP::set_multicast_send_interface(const String &p_if_name) {\n+\tERR_FAIL_COND_V(_sock.is_null(), ERR_UNAVAILABLE);\n+    ERR_FAIL_COND_V(!_sock.is_valid(), ERR_UNCONFIGURED);","path":"core/io/packet_peer_udp.cpp","commit_id":"99f71b3d50c60391a276505778d3daadcf9b70da","original_commit_id":"99f71b3d50c60391a276505778d3daadcf9b70da","user":{"login":"alexfacciorusso","id":4479527,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0Nzk1Mjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4479527?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexfacciorusso","html_url":"https://github.com/alexfacciorusso","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexfacciorusso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexfacciorusso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexfacciorusso/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexfacciorusso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexfacciorusso/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexfacciorusso/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexfacciorusso/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexfacciorusso/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexfacciorusso/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Hey guys! I just thougth to add what I think here (premise: I have been in software development for 18+ years). Also, please do not take my comment as specifically defending OP or offending (quite the opposite!) maintainers, NOR directly relates to this PR; I just happened to open this PR and read its comments.\r\n\r\nAlso, I am not expert with the internals of Godot, but I hope to open a sane discussion about this. Mind, I **won't** use any AI to generate **any part** of this answer just to prove my point.\r\n\r\n@AThousandShips as a human developer, by looking at the cpp API, I really see how either an agent OR a human could get confused by `is_null` vs `is_valid`, plus I'm trying to understand your comment saying `_sock.is_null()` is the same as `!_sock.is_valid()`:\r\n\r\n```\r\n_FORCE_INLINE_ bool is_valid() const { return is_inet() || is_unix(); }\r\n```\r\n\r\nthis is not just checking if it's null, so saying that `is_null` and `!is_valid` are the same isn't completely true, is it?\r\n\r\nForget for a second AIs exist. If I, as a human (before agents became quite smart in the recent months/years) had seen that API, I probably for the sake of being 100% sure, would have done both of those checks.\r\n\r\nPlus, OP seemed to have thrown two different errors on those checks, which sounds reasonable to me: if it's null, throw UNAVAILABLE, otherwise, throw UNCONFIGURED (e.g. that sock is not null but it's unconfigured). As a developer, to me those two errors/exceptions quite make sense to be separate (again, I don't know the internals, but the check seemed sound).\r\n\r\nWhat I'm trying to say is: if the API isn't clear (having two different methods `is_null` and `!is_valid` that, by reading your review, \"do the same\") then why being defensive if a contributor or their AI agent checks both, unless it actually affects performance (and if it does, it should be added in the c code as a method documentation)? From a **human coder** point of view, `is_valid` and `is_null` have two very different meanings, and probably I also would have checked both.\r\n\r\nTwo issues here I'm seeing around on GitHub in these days: over-defensiveness (sometimes justified, sometimes totally prejudiced) against AI-aided contributions, hurting both human coders AND the code their agents produce with genuine mistakes even a human would have done, and \"you are mistaken because you use AI\" vs \"actually, this API is not perfect and I see how that issue could have happened to a new human contributor\".\r\n\r\nIn my experience across multiple fields, if an AI can mistake around a public API, it's usually API's fault (e.g. unclear or unexisting documentation, wrong naming, obsolete methods that haven't been made deprecated etc), and asking developers to read the whole documentation available somewhere else aside from in code about every little is a bit unreasonable in any professional or non-professional setting!\r\n\r\nPlease, take this comment as my own contribution to start a constructive conversation, we are all smart people and if we feel this comment has offended in any way, just ignore it instead of transforming it in a battle ground. Thanks 🙏🏻 ","created_at":"2026-04-26T14:23:54Z","updated_at":"2026-04-26T14:23:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118964#discussion_r3143618635","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118964","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3143618635"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118964#discussion_r3143618635"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118964"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3143618635/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":73,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3143470195,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3143626456","pull_request_review_id":4177034082,"id":3143626456,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc67X-7Y","diff_hunk":"@@ -68,6 +68,30 @@ Error PacketPeerUDP::leave_multicast_group(IPAddress p_multi_address, const Stri\n \treturn _sock->leave_multicast_group(p_multi_address, p_if_name);\n }\n \n+Error PacketPeerUDP::set_multicast_send_interface(const String &p_if_name) {\n+\tERR_FAIL_COND_V(_sock.is_null(), ERR_UNAVAILABLE);\n+    ERR_FAIL_COND_V(!_sock.is_valid(), ERR_UNCONFIGURED);","path":"core/io/packet_peer_udp.cpp","commit_id":"99f71b3d50c60391a276505778d3daadcf9b70da","original_commit_id":"99f71b3d50c60391a276505778d3daadcf9b70da","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"That's not the code though? It's `!_sock.is_valid()` which *is* the opposite, you probably meant `!_sock->is_valid()` which is *completely* different, and isn't even correct either, you probably meant the method on `Address` *insi